    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05f163a0_eac68a07",
        "filename": "zephyr/cmake/toolchain/llvm/target.cmake",
        "patchSetId": 36
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-26T17:40:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This may be a little risky because we may accidentally add code that ends up calling a builtin function that uses floating point. (Or when the compiler is updated it may start calling those builtins for some code as an optimization.)\n\nSince the code has to be executed for us to see a fault, it may not show up in normal testing if it\u0027s in an obscure code path. The safest way would be to check that the generated code does not contain any floating-point instructions.\n\nWe could add something like this to the cmake build (untested):\n\n```\narm-none-eabi-objdump -d ec.*.elf | grep -w -E \"v(add|sub|mul|div|ldr|str|mov|cmp)[.]f(32|64)\"\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a5beb85f_a1d4f9fb",
      "revId": "ab354800e8f28f2b73085f352e632bd0cf9450b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17e5ef02_81fb986a",
        "filename": "zephyr/cmake/toolchain/llvm/target.cmake",
        "patchSetId": 36
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-27T11:25:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally, I agree 100%. I\u0027m still thinking how we can handle this in a better way. \n\nI\u0027m not fully familiar with the toolchain ebuilds, but I\u0027m thinking of something like this: add a new ebuild to build the second version libraries, with floating point operations disabled. Then, in the project files/here force the linker to use those libraries instead of the current ones?",
      "parentUuid": "05f163a0_eac68a07",
      "revId": "ab354800e8f28f2b73085f352e632bd0cf9450b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
